@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title Tutorial 1 · State diagram: who destroys one synthetic Card?
top to bottom direction
skinparam roundcorner 18
hide empty description
state "Program has no Card\nNothing to destroy" as absent
state "Program owns a live Card\nProgram is responsible for destroying it" as live
state "Library is running destroy_card\nLibrary has taken responsibility" as destroying
state "Library has destroyed the Card\nCard lifetime has ended" as dead
absent -[bold]-> absent : create_card returns null:\nprogram sees allocation failure
absent -[bold]-> live : create_card returns a Card:\nprogram receives ownership
live -[bold]-> destroying : destroy_card begins:\nprogram transfers responsibility (consume)
destroying -[bold]-> dead : library destroys the Card\nbefore returning
legend bottom
  Start at the top and follow the labelled arrows.
  Rounded box = Card state and who must destroy it; bold arrow = change of state.
  The loop returns to the same state after allocation failure.
  Program = caller; library = callee. Both creation results are valid to inspect.
  Non-normative: C2, C3, C5. This view covers Card lifetime only.
  Label access is shown in part 2. Eventual return is not promised.
endlegend
@enduml
